==Latin==

===Etymology===
From  {{proto|Indo-European|dómh₂os|lang=la}}. Cognates include Ancient Greek {{term|δόμος|sc=polytonic|tr=dómos|lang=grc}} and Sanskrit {{term|दम|tr=dáma|lang=sa|sc=Deva}}. Confer the German ''[[Zimmer]]'' ("room") and English ''[[timber]]''.

===Noun===
'''domus''', {{f}} ('''[[Appendix:Latin fourth declension|4th declension]]''', irregular)

# a [[house]], a [[home]]

